.TH "Williams Students Online" "1" "24 January 2025" "2.0" "wso-backend man page"
.SH NAME
wso-backend \- run the WSO server 
.SH SYNOPSIS
wso-backend [--config] [--development] [--verbose]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Running
wso-backend
starts the server for WSO, which will open port 8080 and begin accepting requests. For more information please read the documentation at \c
.UR https://github.com/WilliamsStudentsOnline/wso-go
the project's GitHub
.UE \c
\ page\&.

.SH OPTIONS
The options for
wso-backend
are as follows:
.TP
\-\-config
Take the first argument as a file with a valid configuration file for the server\&.
.TP
\-\-development
Enable development mode, with more log messages\&.

.SH SEE ALSO
See the \c
.UR https://wso-dev.williams.edu/api/docs/index.html
API documentation
.UE \c
\ for more information\&.
.SH BUGS
Yes. See the issue tracker for more information.
.SH AUTHOR
Williams Students Online
